        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A methanol solution of Dy(PhCOO) (0.10 mmol, 0.0536 g) was added to H2L (0.11 mmol, 0.0214 g) dissolved in 10 mL of methanol. The mixture was stirred for 30 min, then Ni(ClO4)2·6H2O (0.0443 g, 0.12 mmol) and triethylamine (0.3 mmol) were added. The resulting deep-yellow solution was stirred for 3 h. Block brown single crystals suitable for X-ray diffraction were obtained after 6 d.",
