      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Dc susceptibility (1000 Oe, 2–300 K) shows χMT = 46.25 cm3 K mol−1 at room temperature, decreasing to 30.55 cm3 K mol−1 at 2 K. Magnetization at 2 K reaches 27.10 μB at 7 T without saturation; M vs H/T curves are non-superimposed, consistent with anisotropy and/or low-lying excited states. Zero-field ac susceptibility shows frequency-dependent out-of-phase signals below 4 K (no χ″ peaks), indicating slow magnetization relaxation with a small barrier and possible SMM behavior.",
