        "summary": "Diamagnetic YIII; magnetism arises from NiII. χMT = 6.16 cm3 K mol−1 at room temperature, rises to 7.66 cm3 K mol−1 at 30 K (ferromagnetic Ni···Ni), then falls to 2.07 cm3 K mol−1 at 2 K (ZFS of NiII). Fit of a two-J plus D Hamiltonian gave J1 = 7.6 cm−1, J2 = 6.2 cm−1, g = 2.19, D = 19.1 cm−1. Magnetization 8.05 μB at 2 K and 7 T, near saturation. No out-of-phase ac signal.",
